WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.012 --> 00:00:01.470
METE ATAMEL:
Text-to-Speech API can

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:05.070
be used to convert text
into natural-sounding audio.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.980
Let's see how to use
Text-to-Speech with C-sharp.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.160
First, make sure the API
is enabled in your project,

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.650
and a service account
exists to make API calls.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.530
Both are explained in the
call lab in the video notes.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:20.970
In Cloud Shell, let's create a
simple .NET console lab and add

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:24.230
Text-to-Speech API Nugget
package to the project.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.645
Open the Online Code Editor
and navigate to program.cs.

00:00:27.645 --> 00:00:30.390
We will convert a piece
of text to speech.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.030
Reference to Text-to-Speech
API Perry library.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.010
Create a Text-to-Speech client.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.140
Specify the text
we want to convert.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.810
Specify voice
selection parameters.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.570
And use MP3 as the audio format.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:46.140
Finally, code synthesized
speech on the input.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:51.740
And save the result
to an MP3 file.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.030
Let's run the app.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.020
There you go.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.710
You just create a speech from
text using Text-to-Speech API.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:01.060
You can download and listen
the MP3 file if you like.

